title: Global Pragma Definitions
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

Both customisation styles (marker tiddlers and `\custom` pragmas) have a wiki-wide form. With the vocabulary engine in v1.0, the wiki-wide path is just "a vocabulary you activate". The pre-v1 global-pragma mechanism is preserved as an escape hatch.

!! Option 1: vocabularies (canonical, wiki-wide markers)

A marker tiddler tagged with a vocabulary tag (e.g. `vocab/default`, `vocab/color-boxes`) plus a vocabulary meta tiddler is automatically wiki-wide. Any tiddler that activates the vocabulary via its type field gets the markers:

```
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki;vocab=Default,Color-Boxes
```

No `\importcustom`, no PageTemplate edit. See [[Vocabulary Engine]] for the field schema.

!! Option 2: global pragmas (escape hatch, pragma-based)

If you prefer to express your wiki-wide rules as `\custom` pragmas instead of marker tiddlers, the plugin keeps a system tiddler that's loaded into every parser as a pragma source:

''$:/config/custom-markup/pragma/PageTemplate''

This tiddler is tagged <<tag $:/tags/Macro>>. It contains:

```
\importcustom [tag[$:/tags/Pragma]]
```

That means: every tiddler tagged <<tag $:/tags/Pragma>> has its `\custom` pragmas imported into every parser. Define one tiddler per topic, tag it `$:/tags/Pragma`, and its pragmas become wiki-wide.

''Important.'' If your pragma tiddler also defines `\procedure` or `\define` macros, you ''have to'' tag it with both <<tag $:/tags/Pragma>> and <<tag $:/tags/Macro>>. Otherwise the macros are not visible at render time.

!!! Existing global pragma tiddlers

<<list-links "[tag[$:/tags/Pragma]]">>

!!! Tag - <<tag "$:/tags/Macro">>

Tiddlers tagged this way are evaluated in TW core's [[$:/core/ui/PageTemplate]]. This is what makes pragmas defined in [[$:/config/custom-markup/pragma/PageTemplate]] available everywhere.

!!! Tag - <<tag "$:/tags/Pragma">>

The tag <<tag "$:/tags/Pragma">> is defined by the custom-markup plugin. The sort order of tiddlers tagged this way decides who wins on key collisions: ''the last definition wins.''

!! Cache invalidation

The plugin caches the parsed output of [[$:/config/custom-markup/pragma/PageTemplate]] per wiki. The cache is invalidated when ''PageTemplate itself'' changes. Editing a `\custom` pragma inside a `$:/tags/Pragma`-tagged tiddler does ''not'' invalidate the cache. Workaround until you reload: open PageTemplate and save it (no edit needed) to force a re-parse.

!! Required entry point

The title [[$:/config/custom-markup/pragma/PageTemplate]] is hardcoded in the plugin as the global-pragma entry point. ''Do not rename or delete this tiddler.'' If it is missing, global pragmas stop loading silently (no error, no warning) and any `\custom` pragmas defined in `$:/tags/Pragma`-tagged tiddlers stop applying. To restore: re-add a tiddler with that exact title, tag it <<tag $:/tags/Macro>>, and put `\importcustom [tag[$:/tags/Pragma]]` in its body.

!! When to use which

* Vocabulary: structured, schema-driven, easy to opt in per tiddler. Best for new code.
* Global pragma: useful when you want to keep a body of v0.x-style `\custom` definitions wiki-wide without converting them to marker tiddlers. Also useful when the customization is tied to a TW macro defined in the same tiddler.

See [[Pragma - importcustom]] for the `\importcustom` pragma itself.
